<b>Episode 7: "A Year in My Life"</b>

02:39.290 --> 02:42.140
<b>Episode 7: "A Year in My Life"</b>

02:39.320 --> 02:42.140
<b>Episode 7: "A Year in My Life"</b>

02:39.350 --> 02:42.140
<b>Episode 7: "A Year in My Life"</b>

02:39.380 --> 02:42.140
<b>Episode 7: "A Year in My Life"</b>

02:42.400 --> 02:44.060
That customer's been waiting a while.

02:44.060 --> 02:44.890
Got it.

02:45.400 --> 02:48.300
It's a huge help having you here for backup.

02:48.300 --> 02:51.350
With so many customers, 
I lose track of what order to serve them in.

02:52.320 --> 02:55.940
Well, that's rare. 
You don't give compliments often.

02:55.940 --> 02:59.260
We do have a lot more customers now, though.

02:59.260 --> 03:01.820
More than when Grandma was here, even!

03:02.560 --> 03:04.990
Probably because of the 
uniforms you made for us.

03:05.290 --> 03:05.990
Huh?

03:06.670 --> 03:09.690
I've been getting lots of comments 
on the street lately.

03:09.690 --> 03:12.600
They're like, "She's from 
that café with the cute uniforms!"

03:12.960 --> 03:16.210
Really? Who said that? 
Did they say anything else?

03:16.700 --> 03:19.030
Thanks for dinner!

03:19.470 --> 03:24.040
Well, I'm kinda tired, so I'm gonna 
take my bath first and go to bed.

03:24.720 --> 03:27.930
Hey, wanna borrow my rubber duckie?

03:27.930 --> 03:29.820
It'll make your bath more fun!

03:31.100 --> 03:32.790
Maybe I will, then.

03:33.850 --> 03:35.610
<b>Ami</b>

03:34.450 --> 03:38.910
You know, Akane-chan seems different lately.

03:38.910 --> 03:42.450
Yeah. She used to be pretty unapproachable.

03:42.450 --> 03:45.560
She does seem a lot less prickly now.

03:45.950 --> 03:48.990
Well, we've all been 
living together for a year.

03:48.990 --> 03:51.220
She's an important part of the family now.

03:55.190 --> 03:57.770
Family, huh?

04:01.580 --> 04:03.630
You're still doing this every day?

04:03.630 --> 04:05.180
I'm impressed.

04:05.950 --> 04:09.040
You've been doing it almost daily 
since we reopened.

04:09.790 --> 04:13.060
People's tastes change with the seasons.

04:14.560 --> 04:16.440
<i>And that's why...</i>

04:17.300 --> 04:21.440
I check the flavor myself the day before.

04:21.870 --> 04:25.690
To make sure the coffee I serve 
always tastes the same.

04:28.850 --> 04:31.830
You really are Grandma's grandson.

04:32.270 --> 04:34.280
You're so much like her.

04:36.000 --> 04:38.670
Are you thinking of quitting this job?

04:41.200 --> 04:43.720
Wh-What makes you think that?

04:44.170 --> 04:46.640
No reason. Just had a hunch.

04:47.120 --> 04:50.400
You've been going around complimenting 
everyone. It's not like you.

04:50.400 --> 04:54.020
It felt creepy, so I was trying 
to figure out why.

04:54.600 --> 04:57.620
Based on your reaction, I guess I'm right.

04:58.480 --> 05:00.320
So you'll be moving out, then?

05:01.030 --> 05:02.680
Leaving this house?

05:04.680 --> 05:06.820
Call it family circumstances.

05:07.270 --> 05:09.780
I'm thinking I'll be out by this weekend.

05:10.080 --> 05:12.570
I won't need my pay for this month.

05:12.570 --> 05:15.910
You can use it to get rid 
of the stuff in my room.

05:17.170 --> 05:18.970
Okay, will do.

05:19.500 --> 05:21.800
I owe a lot to you.

05:24.000 --> 05:27.160
Since it's my last week... 
wanna give mine a squeeze?

05:28.120 --> 05:30.420
Be gentle, though.

05:34.130 --> 05:35.640
I was joking.

05:35.640 --> 05:37.770
If it embarrasses you 
that much, don't say it.

05:39.060 --> 05:41.790
Am I that unattractive?

05:41.790 --> 05:44.360
I did have a lot of male fans, 
I'll have you know.

05:45.320 --> 05:46.860
So your band gets past tense, too?

05:50.280 --> 05:52.200
Well, boobs aside...

05:52.200 --> 05:54.330
If you feel like you owe me,

05:54.330 --> 05:56.430
there is one thing I'd like you to do.

05:56.430 --> 05:57.210
Huh?

05:57.210 --> 05:59.590
Tomorrow's the café's day off.

06:00.060 --> 06:01.930
Go on a date with me.

06:09.570 --> 06:12.300
Hayato-kun and Akane-chan 
are going on a date?!

06:12.300 --> 06:16.680
Yes! They said they were going out 
on a rainy day like this,

06:16.680 --> 06:20.440
so I asked why, and they said 
it was a date! A <i>date</i>!

06:20.440 --> 06:24.320
You're kidding, right?! 
Did they have that kind of relationship?!

06:24.320 --> 06:27.870
I can't imagine Hayato-kun 
making a move on her,

06:27.870 --> 06:30.450
so it must've been Akane-chan who asked?

06:31.480 --> 06:34.750
C-Come to think of it, 
she did say she might be willing...

06:34.750 --> 06:36.080
with Hayato-kun.

06:36.080 --> 06:37.410
True...

06:38.920 --> 06:40.300
I see.

06:40.300 --> 06:43.360
Outside air in winter makes 
cups and servers cold,

06:43.360 --> 06:45.190
so we should warm them up.

06:46.090 --> 06:48.910
I wondered what you meant 
when you called this a "date."

06:48.910 --> 06:50.220
I'm just giving you info?

06:50.220 --> 06:52.000
What choice did we have?

06:52.000 --> 06:55.560
It'd be a pain to discuss this at home 
with all the others there.

06:55.560 --> 06:58.230
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

06:55.560 --> 06:58.230
<b>Restock washcloths 
One cup is cracked 

No particular problems currently 
Private event reservations at Familia 
Don't turn on lights late at night 
Outside air in winter makes
 cups and servers cold</b>

06:55.930 --> 06:58.230
You're free to quit the café if you want,

06:58.540 --> 07:00.990
but I need you to tell me these things first,

07:00.990 --> 07:02.730
or our business will suffer.

07:03.560 --> 07:04.820
Oh, I see.

07:04.820 --> 07:07.210
What're you so grouchy for?

07:07.210 --> 07:10.070
Were you hoping to see 
a movie or go shopping?

07:10.070 --> 07:13.850
I'm willing to do that, 
if you ask like you mean it.

07:14.280 --> 07:17.450
I'm not asking you for a damn thing!

07:17.970 --> 07:21.830
Well? Did Grandma say anything else?

07:22.740 --> 07:26.340
<i>Of course, no matter how good 
you make the coffee,</i>

07:26.900 --> 07:31.420
it doesn't mean a thing 
if the drinker's heart isn't in it.

07:32.640 --> 07:35.750
If there's something troubling you, 
tell me about it.

07:36.530 --> 07:38.850
I'm here to listen.

07:41.890 --> 07:43.260
I...

07:47.640 --> 07:51.020
I don't have anything more to tell you.

07:52.600 --> 07:53.700
Okay.

07:54.160 --> 07:55.910
Let's go home, then.

07:56.520 --> 07:57.290
Sure.

07:57.870 --> 08:01.120
So where do you think those two went?!

08:01.120 --> 08:03.740
Well, they picked a rainy day to go out!

08:03.740 --> 08:05.750
So it couldn't be an amusement park, right?

08:05.750 --> 08:07.370
Maybe a concert?

08:07.370 --> 08:10.270
Hayato-kun seems to like bands and stuff.

08:10.270 --> 08:11.610
You know...

08:12.010 --> 08:17.500
I overheard Hayacchi and Akane-san 
talking at the café yesterday...

08:18.350 --> 08:20.730
Why can't we go in through the front door?

08:22.520 --> 08:25.400
The coffee at that place 
we went to was gross,

08:25.400 --> 08:28.410
so I thought I'd have you make me a cup.

08:29.550 --> 08:30.780
Sure, I guess...

08:33.250 --> 08:38.370
This'll probably be the last time 
I make you coffee, you know.

08:38.370 --> 08:39.450
Yeah.

08:39.820 --> 08:41.740
I'll be sure to take note of the flavor.

08:45.170 --> 08:48.380
It only lasted a year, but it's been fun.

08:48.960 --> 08:51.710
My time living here will be a good memory.

08:51.710 --> 08:53.010
Yeah?

08:53.010 --> 08:56.540
I feel bad for what I did 
to my bandmates, though.

08:56.540 --> 08:58.510
Telling them out of the blue 
that I was quitting...

08:58.960 --> 09:01.020
I think that was a shame, too.

09:01.020 --> 09:03.900
The song you wrote was really good.

09:12.690 --> 09:13.690
Hey...

09:14.310 --> 09:18.320
Why aren't you asking why I'm 
moving back to my family home?

09:18.320 --> 09:19.370
Huh?

09:22.400 --> 09:24.290
Guess you wouldn't be interested, huh?

09:24.920 --> 09:29.060
As far as you're concerned, 
I'm just pretend family.

09:31.140 --> 09:34.980
Would you ask someone anything 
as long as they were family?

09:37.280 --> 09:39.310
If you don't want to tell me, I won't ask,

09:39.310 --> 09:41.700
and if you've made up your mind, 
I won't stop you.

09:41.700 --> 09:45.930
No matter who I'm dealing with, 
I respect their wishes.

09:46.580 --> 09:48.410
Even if they're family.

09:50.660 --> 09:52.120
That's so you.

09:54.360 --> 09:58.000
I come from a reputable family 
that's been around for over 200 years.

09:58.000 --> 09:59.950
They run a trading business.

10:00.470 --> 10:02.910
But my dad died young,

10:02.910 --> 10:05.020
and I'm the only one who can carry it on.

10:05.620 --> 10:10.470
So they're ordering me to join the company, 
take a husband, and have an heir.

10:11.600 --> 10:14.000
They've already decided who I'll be marrying.

10:14.320 --> 10:17.470
Hilarious, right? I've never even met him.

10:18.020 --> 10:21.600
I told them to at least let me do 
what I wanted for one year,

10:21.600 --> 10:23.970
and started the band and the café work...

10:24.700 --> 10:28.640
But then my mother called, saying, 
"That's enough. Come home."

10:24.970 --> 10:26.810
<b></b>Mother

10:30.480 --> 10:33.790
I mean, I've done my own thing for long enough,

10:33.790 --> 10:36.310
so I figured it was fine.

10:36.860 --> 10:40.780
I do kind of have a responsibility 
to the family I was born into.

10:43.830 --> 10:45.120
You know...

10:46.280 --> 10:48.120
I get the gist now,

10:48.550 --> 10:50.920
but don't say things you don't mean.

10:51.570 --> 10:54.540
I hate being lied to.

10:56.160 --> 10:58.720
Wh-What makes you think I'm lying?

11:00.220 --> 11:02.490
The coffee tastes like shit.

11:05.030 --> 11:06.680
No!

11:06.680 --> 11:09.470
Don't move out, Akane-san!

11:09.470 --> 11:10.800
You can't do that!

11:10.800 --> 11:11.690
Yeah!

11:11.690 --> 11:13.810
You were eavesdropping again?

11:13.810 --> 11:17.940
And when did this thing about you marrying 
a guy you don't even know come up?

11:17.940 --> 11:19.440
You guys...

11:19.440 --> 11:22.950
We finally got to be friends... 
This is too sad.

11:22.950 --> 11:26.650
I haven't had a chance to see 
one of your concerts yet!

11:26.650 --> 11:27.700
Please don't quit!

11:27.700 --> 11:31.700
I'm worried how Familia's coffee will be 
with only Hayato-kun left to make it!

11:32.370 --> 11:34.250
No! No! No!

11:34.250 --> 11:37.380
I will <i>not</i> have it!

11:38.390 --> 11:39.800
So what'll it be?

11:40.780 --> 11:44.260
If this is your decision, I'll respect it.

11:45.640 --> 11:47.060
I...

11:52.480 --> 11:54.100
I want to stay here.

11:54.850 --> 11:56.540
I don't want to go home.

11:57.660 --> 12:00.220
I want to stay with all of you forever.

12:00.220 --> 12:01.990
I want to stay with my band, too.

12:01.990 --> 12:06.090
And I want to learn to make better coffee.

12:08.480 --> 12:12.870
But there's no way 
my mother's going to allow that.

12:13.470 --> 12:16.500
No matter what I try to do, 
she'll drag me back.

12:17.200 --> 12:18.630
It's all right.

12:19.120 --> 12:23.430
When that time comes, 
I'll do something about it.

12:23.430 --> 12:26.660
You should live the way you want to.

12:35.310 --> 12:36.550
So...

12:38.840 --> 12:41.650
Do something, Hayato!

12:43.750 --> 12:46.300
Okay. I will.

12:49.920 --> 12:53.540
I thought it curious that this café 
had such a young owner.

12:54.350 --> 12:58.340
Now I understand why that is.

12:58.720 --> 13:04.340
It must have been quite challenging 
for your grandmother to raise you.

13:04.340 --> 13:07.150
Yes, I'm sure it was.

13:07.150 --> 13:10.650
What is it that you 
wanted to discuss with me?

13:10.650 --> 13:14.390
I have a vehicle waiting, 
so do keep it brief, please.

13:16.200 --> 13:19.550
It seems Akane-san has something 
she wants to say to you.

13:19.550 --> 13:21.450
Will you hear her out?

13:21.450 --> 13:23.610
What?! <i>I</i> have to say it?

13:25.110 --> 13:26.680
Something you want to say?

13:27.030 --> 13:28.620
U-Um...

13:35.620 --> 13:39.230
I know I said I'd join 
the company after a year,

13:39.230 --> 13:42.380
but there are still things I want to do.

13:42.930 --> 13:45.900
I was hoping 
you could wait a while longer.

13:46.470 --> 13:50.170
Are you referring to your musical activities?

13:50.170 --> 13:53.100
Yeah... And my job.

13:53.890 --> 13:56.810
Then there's nothing to discuss.

13:57.680 --> 14:01.740
You will stop talking nonsense and come home.

14:02.650 --> 14:08.270
Has there ever been anything that you 
started and then stuck with for long?

14:08.270 --> 14:11.910
You always give up 
and leave things unfinished.

14:11.910 --> 14:16.160
That's because you keep forcing me 
to do things I don't want—

14:16.160 --> 14:19.290
I told you that I will not 
abide backtalking or excuses.

14:20.480 --> 14:21.580
Yes, ma'am.

14:22.130 --> 14:26.270
What is that you're wearing, anyway? 
And that hair color?

14:26.270 --> 14:29.760
What a shameful look 
for the Hououji family's heir.

14:29.760 --> 14:33.580
Not to mention the way you've been speaking.

14:33.580 --> 14:36.420
I'd be too embarrassed 
to present you to anyone.

14:37.120 --> 14:40.490
Seeing you right now gives me 
a painfully clear picture

14:40.490 --> 14:43.960
of how useless and wasteful 
this past year has been for you.

14:48.330 --> 14:51.980
I told you to flick your wrist
 when whisking tea.

14:53.260 --> 14:56.580
How many times must I tell you, Akane-san?

14:56.580 --> 15:00.150
I'm sorry. I'm sorry, Mother.

15:01.120 --> 15:02.750
I... I'm...

15:02.750 --> 15:03.690
Hey.

15:04.360 --> 15:05.960
Isn't that quite enough?

15:07.320 --> 15:09.790
Why won't you say anything back to her?

15:09.790 --> 15:10.630
Huh?

15:10.960 --> 15:13.620
I thought you didn't want to go home?

15:14.040 --> 15:17.690
The way this is going, 
that's exactly what's gonna happen.

15:17.690 --> 15:19.180
Is that what you want?

15:19.180 --> 15:20.920
O-Of course it's not!

15:20.920 --> 15:23.940
Then why are you clamming up? 
Are you that spineless?

15:23.940 --> 15:25.160
I did tell her!

15:25.160 --> 15:27.690
You only told her. 
You didn't make her understand.

15:28.030 --> 15:31.240
And what was that, "I was hoping 
you could wait a while longer," anyway?

15:31.240 --> 15:33.640
You're not making it clear 
what you want to do.

15:33.640 --> 15:36.530
You're just putting off 
coming to a conclusion.

15:36.840 --> 15:39.540
Your mom's telling you to come home

15:39.840 --> 15:42.630
because your half-assed 
behavior worries her.

15:44.740 --> 15:49.630
Well, what are <i>you</i> trying to pull, 
sitting here silent all this time?!

15:50.600 --> 15:53.100
Weren't you going to do something 
about this for me?!

15:53.100 --> 15:57.140
You talked big, but now that 
my mom's here, you just watch quietly?!

15:57.610 --> 16:01.390
Quit bitching! 
Whose life are we talking about?!

16:02.890 --> 16:09.900
Why should I help someone who can't look 
her own mother in the eye and tell her no?!

16:10.190 --> 16:13.050
What was the point of 
that year of your life?!

16:13.050 --> 16:15.920
If that's as far as your determination goes,

16:15.920 --> 16:17.530
just quit everything!

16:17.930 --> 16:21.400
Go home and inherit the business 
or get married or whatever!

16:30.280 --> 16:33.850
Yeah. You're exactly right.

16:36.040 --> 16:40.220
I'm sorry, Mother. 
I didn't even serve you tea.

16:40.540 --> 16:42.570
You also like coffee, right?

16:42.570 --> 16:44.150
Huh? Yes...

16:44.730 --> 16:46.890
Don't tell me <i>you're</i> going to make it?

16:47.920 --> 16:50.820
I am. Please wait just a few minutes.

16:53.570 --> 16:56.160
I have investigated the matter, masters.

16:56.160 --> 16:58.350
And how did it look?

16:58.350 --> 16:59.030
Zoom!

16:59.030 --> 17:01.020
It looked awful!

17:01.020 --> 17:04.660
Hayacchi told Akane-san to just quit!

17:04.660 --> 17:08.670
What does that mean?! 
He said he'd do something about it for her!

17:08.940 --> 17:11.800
He must've chickened out 
'cause her mom's so scary!

17:11.800 --> 17:14.120
You can't be that way, Hayato-kun!

17:14.120 --> 17:15.300
That coward!

17:15.610 --> 17:18.650
I can't leave this to that phony blowhard!

17:18.650 --> 17:20.220
Yeah!

17:21.040 --> 17:24.460
Half of a cup of coffee's flavor can be 
attributed to the quality of the beans.

17:24.460 --> 17:28.660
The other half comes from 
the barista's technique.

17:30.130 --> 17:34.570
How can a girl who couldn't make 
a proper cup of tea be so skilled?

17:38.240 --> 17:42.700
Yes, that's it. You've gotten much better.

17:42.700 --> 17:45.220
That's right. Slowly and carefully.

17:46.420 --> 17:49.400
These beans need forty seconds to bloom.

17:49.960 --> 17:53.530
Any longer than that, 
and it'll taste sour and wrong.

17:54.400 --> 17:56.360
<i>Yeah. I know.</i>

17:56.360 --> 17:59.720
Be careful not to pour the hot water 
directly onto the filter.

17:57.800 --> 17:59.720
...onto the filter.

18:00.540 --> 18:03.290
Pour slowly, in a spiral pattern.

18:04.890 --> 18:07.580
I learned all that from her.

18:11.250 --> 18:18.230
Hououji Akane is the waitress who makes 
the best coffee of anyone in this café.

18:21.930 --> 18:23.610
Thank you for waiting.

18:26.540 --> 18:29.120
This is the result of my past year.

18:29.120 --> 18:31.540
Please enjoy.

18:32.240 --> 18:36.060
I see. This is the result of your one year, then?

18:37.080 --> 18:37.860
Yes.

18:42.120 --> 18:43.530
May I say one thing?

18:44.770 --> 18:47.420
No matter how good someone's coffee is,

18:47.420 --> 18:51.560
it doesn't mean a thing 
if the drinker's heart isn't in it.

18:52.690 --> 18:56.840
Just for this one time, at least, 
could you focus only on the flavor?

19:01.760 --> 19:03.880
Yes, I will.

19:12.080 --> 19:17.260
When I was young, I traveled 
around the world as a diplomat.

19:17.890 --> 19:20.810
As the only child born to the Hououji family,

19:20.810 --> 19:24.400
I was often told that I would 
one day inherit the business,

19:24.400 --> 19:28.830
but at the time, I found pleasure 
and fulfillment in the job I had,

19:28.830 --> 19:32.900
so I couldn't even bring myself 
to think about inheriting.

19:33.570 --> 19:37.510
That said, Akane-san, you aren't like I was.

19:38.170 --> 19:41.080
You spend every day wasting 
your life on pointless nonsense,

19:41.080 --> 19:45.360
never even trying to get a proper job.

19:45.360 --> 19:47.240
It's absolutely disgraceful.

19:47.870 --> 19:50.400
If that's how you're going to live your life,

19:50.400 --> 19:54.620
it would be better for you if I forced you 
to join our family business.

19:56.800 --> 19:58.520
At least, that's what I thought.

20:06.400 --> 20:10.830
Yes... This coffee is most excellent indeed.

20:11.560 --> 20:13.940
That is all I need to know.

20:14.980 --> 20:18.940
Akane-san, live your life as you see fit.

20:27.320 --> 20:28.970
Thank you.

20:30.570 --> 20:35.420
Incidentally, I have yet to learn 
the name of this café's owner.

20:36.540 --> 20:39.800
Oh, sorry about that. I'm Kasukabe Hayato.

20:41.010 --> 20:44.800
I see. It certainly is a small world.

20:45.210 --> 20:46.260
What?

20:47.800 --> 20:49.310
Ma'am!

20:49.770 --> 20:54.040
You can't make Akane-chan 
marry someone she doesn't love!

20:54.040 --> 20:56.060
Let her live the way she wants!

20:56.060 --> 20:58.200
Yeah! You can't force her!

20:58.200 --> 20:59.880
Would you guys just wait—

21:02.990 --> 21:05.530
This café needs Akane-chan!

21:05.530 --> 21:06.640
That's right!

21:06.640 --> 21:07.680
Please!

21:07.680 --> 21:08.700
Ma'am!

21:11.250 --> 21:14.730
Everything's okay now. 
We're finished talking.

21:14.730 --> 21:15.750
Huh?

21:16.170 --> 21:20.250
Thanks to Hayato, I get to live here again.

21:20.710 --> 21:22.560
Oh... Really?

21:22.560 --> 21:25.680
Well, how about that? 
Hayato-kun really did put in the work.

21:25.680 --> 21:27.930
Way to go, Hayacchi!

21:29.970 --> 21:33.520
Yikes! We were stepping all over him!

21:34.760 --> 21:38.150
I'll turn down your arranged marriage offer.

21:38.150 --> 21:39.270
Thank you.

21:39.830 --> 21:43.230
I'll find the one I want to marry on my own.

21:43.960 --> 21:44.890
Oh?

21:45.610 --> 21:48.490
Hayato-kun is a good, diligent boy, isn't he?

21:49.530 --> 21:52.280
I'm sure it won't be easy 
with so many rivals,

21:52.280 --> 21:54.980
but as a Hououji woman, you'd better win.

21:56.560 --> 21:57.710
Huh?!

21:57.710 --> 22:00.540
I-It's not like that!

22:00.920 --> 22:03.340
You're such an open book, really.

22:03.340 --> 22:05.310
So very easy to read.

22:07.790 --> 22:09.460
Mother!

22:20.370 --> 22:22.180
You're out here again?

22:22.520 --> 22:25.400
I've been looking for you. Dinner's ready.

22:25.400 --> 22:26.900
Let's go, Hayato.

22:27.780 --> 22:30.240
Oh, okay.

22:31.140 --> 22:34.810
Thanks for being there today. I owe you.

22:34.810 --> 22:35.750
For what?

22:36.370 --> 22:39.240
If you hadn't yelled at me,

22:39.240 --> 22:42.820
I might never have had 
the guts to defy my mother.

22:44.040 --> 22:48.880
Actually, I was holding back a lot 
since your mom was there.

22:49.280 --> 22:52.520
Normally, I would've really let you have it.

22:53.120 --> 22:55.900
But anyway, I'm glad it worked out.

22:56.780 --> 23:01.020
Now I'll be able to drink 
your coffee for a while longer.

23:01.880 --> 23:04.200
Your attitude and expression suck,

23:04.200 --> 23:06.330
but coffee's the one thing you get right.

23:07.090 --> 23:08.360
Oh, really?

23:09.220 --> 23:11.630
You really are adorable, Hayato.

23:11.630 --> 23:12.700
Huh?

23:15.570 --> 23:19.940
You don't need to worry. 
I'll make you coffee all your life.

23:29.090 --> 23:32.170
Don't mock your boss!

23:33.010 --> 23:35.370
Let's go! Dinner's on!

23:42.020 --> 23:57.030
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

23:42.020 --> 23:57.030
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

23:42.410 --> 23:45.790
So Akane-chan used to be 
a proper young lady with undyed hair?

23:45.790 --> 23:48.530
If not for her band, her character 
might've overlapped with Kiku-chan's.

23:48.530 --> 23:49.820
Don't worry!

23:49.820 --> 23:52.280
With a little booze, 
Shiragiku-san gets super hor—

23:52.540 --> 23:54.080
Stop, Ami-chan!

23:54.080 --> 23:56.460
Were you about to say 
something really weird?!
